@@ -120,15 +120,28 @@ A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a
 
 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The directory is published twice: as a page for readers, and in machine-readable form for other software. Both are supported surfaces, and both narrow the directory to one named specialty on request. A reader who names a specialty sees only the veterinarians holding it. The name is matched in full and letter case is disregarded, so part of a name matches nothing. Naming no specialty, or naming one that is empty or only spaces, gives the whole directory. The specialty is named in the address alone; neither surface offers a control for choosing one `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the directory page is opened naming it, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from the held one only by letter case, when the directory page is opened naming it, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given part of a specialty's name, when the directory page is opened naming it, then no veterinarian matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory page is opened naming it, then the page is shown with no veterinarian listed rather than reported as a failure.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a named specialty whose matches span more than one page, when a further page is opened from the directory, then the same specialty still applies.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty named, or one that is empty or only spaces, when the directory page is opened, then every veterinarian is listed as before.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the machine-readable directory, when it is opened naming a specialty, then it carries only the veterinarians holding it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the machine-readable directory, when it is opened naming no specialty, then it carries every veterinarian as before.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears only when no specialty is named.
+3. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears whenever any one of them is named.
 
-**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
